  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 239 AM EDT Wed Oct 7 2026\n\n- Mostly Dry Into The Weekend\n\nWithin the northwest flow today we'll see the shortwave trough\nthis morning exit the area with skies clearing out for the\nafternoon. Tonight we'll see another shortwave bringing cloud \ncover and potentially some sprinkles or light showers. Confidence \nwas not high enough to add to the forecast as showers would be \nshallow and elevated if they developed with little to no \nprecipitation making it to the surface. The best chance would be \nnorth of M-20.\n\nCooler temperatures are expected Thursday with highs in the low to\nmid 60s. Temperatures Thursday night will bring another chance for\nfrost/freeze conditions for portions of north central Michigan.\n\nWhile the forecast is currently dry for Friday. Warm air advection\nwith support of convergence with the low level jet could spark off\nshowers for Friday evening. There is an increase in members with\nmeasurable precipitation Friday evening, therefore would expect \nNBM PoPs to increase with the next run.\n\n- Increasing Chances for Rain Sunday into Next Week\n\nWe'll need to keep an eye on the tropical feature in the Gulf as\nit could bring rainfall to the area Sunday depending on the track.\nOtherwise we'll see a stronger front move through with better\nmoisture for the beginning of next week. This will bring\nadditional chances for rain along with colder temperatures behind\nthe front.",
